# NOTE: gitignore has no inline-comment syntax — a trailing "# ..." on a pattern
# line is taken as literal glob text and matches nothing.  Comments go on their
# own line.

# --- OS / local tooling state ------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.claude/*.lock

# FS-UAE writes a .uaem metadata sidecar next to every file in a directory it
# mounts as an Amiga hard drive (run.sh mounts .run/dh0 + dh1; a WHDLoad test
# mounts wherever you unpack the install), so this one is a global guard.
*.uaem

# --- Copyrighted / captured material: kept LOCAL only, never committed -------
# rof.xex is the original Atari binary (purged from history 2026-06-02); the PNGs
# are game screenshots and comparison captures.  This also covers docs/*.png, so
# a documentation image has to live outside the repo too.  *.rom covers Atari OS /
# Amiga Kickstart images, which land at the repo root as easily as a savestate does.
*.xex
*.png
*.rom

# --- Build output ------------------------------------------------------------
build/
*.o

# --- Generated: regenerable from rof.xex ------------------------------------
# Everything under disasm/ is emitted by tools/ (xex_load.py) or a headless
# Ghidra pass (the Dump*.java scripts); the one CURATED file, symbols.csv (the
# name source of truth), is named back in.  Ignoring the directory rather than
# each output means a new dump does not need a new rule here.
disasm/*
!disasm/symbols.csv
src/gen/rof_gen.c
src/gen/rof_decl.h

# --- Ghidra install + annotation project (never commit) ----------------------
# tools/ghidra has no trailing slash: it is a SYMLINK to a shared install
# (~/.local/share/ghidra), and a trailing-slash pattern only matches a real
# directory, not a symlink to one.
tools/ghidra
tools/ghidra-proj/
tools/__pycache__/

# --- Local scratch: atari800 savestates + RAM dumps --------------------------
# Atari ground-truth captures and scratch working dirs.  Not regenerable from
# anything in the repo (they come from atari800 runs), so they are kept locally
# but never committed.  The loose .a8s/.dat patterns are deliberate: a fresh
# savestate or RAM dump normally lands at the repo root, not in a800dumps/.
/tmp/
/a800dumps/
*.a8s
*.dat
